 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Of course! How old are the kids? Great. A big spot in the grass is easiest with toddlers, so they can see the food and avoid the dirt. Cut them into chunks so they don't choking. Also so the kids can hold one in each hand. Musical chairs, an egg hunt, and a small game of tag keep them busy for hours. A big tent changes the feel of the spot. A white tablecloth makes cleaning up much easier. Yes, and lots of clean water too. A little fruit for a snack is fine, but keep the sugar down. Most important, go easy on the snacks and drinks, so the kids aren't tired at bedtime.",
